id: pm-gantt-chart-mdm1
title: Certify pm-gantt-chart on PM CLI/SDK 2026.10.4 and consolidate pending dependency updates
description: "Dated certification scope: consolidate the PM CLI/SDK 2026.10.4 toolchain and preserve unchanged package gates, clean full and production audits, clean pinned-host health and packed npm/Bun acceptance. PR #128 delivered the toolchain update but its retained receipt reports four high dev-only audit findings, two health advisories and review gaps. PR #141 later removed the dependency chain; that later remediation does not establish the missing dated 2026.10.4 certification acceptance."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: cli,dependencies,release-readiness,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-04T09:32:11.603Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T11:16:25.917Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: "npm run release:check passes with configured coverage thresholds and the unchanged zero-duplication gate; pm health with the repo-pinned 2026.10.4 binary is clean; packed tarball passes real-tracker gantt render/export scenarios via npx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.4 and bunx; pm-github managed extension installed with read-only preview only"
resolution: PR #128 delivered the dated toolchain update; certification remains unestablished.
expected_result: Establish every dated certification acceptance criterion separately from toolchain delivery.
actual_result: "Main 80717afb81f1 contains PR #128 delivery 9a772c1c667f. Its retained 2026.10.4 receipt records release:check 232/232, hostile NODE_PATH 8/8, packed npm/Bun exports for 95 items and production audit 0, but full audit 4 high dev-only findings, two health advisories and review gaps; it explicitly says NOT READY for certification. PR #141 later removes the dependency chain. No later receipt establishes the dated 2026.10.4 certification or current exact-head certification; this item remains in progress."
comments[14]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T09:32:17.384Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "Starting at 7145c6f (Release pm-gantt-chart v2026.09.26). Plan: pm-cli 2026.9.23->2026.10.4, pm-ops->2026.10.4, pm-changelog->2026.9.25, jscpd ^4.3.0->^5.4.0 with #122's zero-dup fixes (shared main-invocation guard, single JSON render, accept-packed PM_PATH isolation), codeql SHA 1c5b6756, @types/node 26.6.4, eslint latest in range; carry #122's pm issue pm-gantt-chart-chso; recopy canonical prepare-merge-driver.ts from pm-ops 2026.10.4; full gate + dogfood + pm-github preview."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T10:12:35.700Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "Real-tracker dogfood PASS. Packed pm-gantt-chart-2026.9.26.tgz installed into a scratch copy of this repo's real .agents/pm and registered via pm package install with CLI 2026.10.4 (capabilities incl. commands/schema). npm path (npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.4): pm gantt renders the full real tracker (19 rows, milestones + TODAY marker); pm gantt --group-by status renders grouped; pm gantt export --format json to stdout and --output gantt.json produce correct window/summary/items (projectStart 2026-05-26); pm gantt export --format svg --output roadmap.svg writes a 41109-byte SVG. bun path (bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.4): pm gantt renders identically (exit 0); gantt export --format json --output gantt-bun.json writes the same JSON. Scratch deleted after evidence capture. Also repaired the carried pm-gantt-chart-chso history chain drift with pm history-repair (pinned CLI 2026.10.4, 9 entries rehashed, verify_ok), clearing the gate_failing history_drift health finding."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T10:13:13.487Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "pm-github installed as managed project extension at latest npm 2026.10.4 (published during this certification; superseding the earlier 2026.9.26 in the same cycle). Read-only previews against unbraind/pm-gantt-chart: pm github validate -> ok (token via gh CLI, HTTP 200, quota 4916/5000); pm github export --dry-run -> plan only, writes nothing; pm github sync --dry-run -> planned 0, no mutation. No issues created/modified, no scheduled sync enabled."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T10:45:06.256Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "CI correction: exact-head CI failed the Duplication gate with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND 'fast-glob' imported from pm-ops/dist/duplication.js. Root cause: pm-ops declares fast-glob as an OPTIONAL peer, but its duplication gate hard-requires it at runtime; this repo's direct fast-glob devDependency exists precisely to satisfy that peer, so removing it broke the gate while my earlier local gate passed only against a stale node_modules (npm install had not pruned it at that point; npm ci is authoritative). fast-glob ^3.3.3 restored; npm ci + full npm run release:check PASS again (duplication-gate 0/9209 lines, 27 sources, 0 clone pairs at threshold 0%). npm audit now reports the same pre-existing dev-only braces (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm) chain that origin/main also reports (main: 7 high; this branch: 4 high - the eslint 10.12/jscpd 5.4 upgrades shrink it), with no patched braces version published, so it is unfixable in-tree without breaking the pm-ops gate; npm audit --omit=dev remains 0 vulnerabilities, which is the gate this repo enforces. Upstream defect to file: pm-ops's fast-glob peer is not actually optional."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T10:58:40.995Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Resumed retained worktree, including the unpushed pi-glm release-provenance commit 5869752. Verified exact-head CI now passes after fast-glob restoration. Finish exact devDependency pins, pm-changelog 2026.10.4, and focused canonical-launcher regressions. Full npm audit remains blocked on GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm: npm braces latest 3.0.3 is affected and fast-glob latest 3.3.3 is required by pm-ops duplication. Record a package follow-up instead of weakening the gate."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:07:23.556Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Resumption validation: clean npm ci and flock-serialized npm run release:check PASS (232/232 tests, 0 skipped; unchanged measured lines/branches/functions thresholds; duplication 0/9239 lines, 27 sources, 0 clones). Launcher suite passed 8/8 with unconditional incomplete/dangling installation and lookup-loop fixtures; canonical launcher unchanged. Real tracker packed dogfood PASS: npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.4 gantt; gantt export --format json --output real.json; gantt export --format svg --output real.svg; bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.4 gantt; gantt export --format json --output real-bun.json; JSON/SVG exports contain 95 items and cmp real.json real-bun.json passes. Scratch deleted. npx pm health ok with stale_in_progress_items:2 advisory. Managed pm-github sync --dry-run --repo unbraind/pm-gantt-chart: planned 0. npm audit --omit=dev: 0; full npm audit: 4 high dev-only reports, blocked on unpublished braces fix (follow-up pm-gantt-chart-e7rd). NOT READY for certification despite green production gates."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:10:24.488Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Applied the cross-repo Windows portability finding proactively: new link fixtures use Node junction type with absolute targets, retaining unconditional execution without privileges needed for directory symbolic links. Linux launcher suite 8/8 and zero-duplication gate pass. Windows runtime not available on this host; canonical launcher unchanged."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:17:15.307Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Review round 2: reproduced CodeRabbit NODE_PATH leakage with NODE_PATH pointing at this checkout node_modules: launcher fixtures fail when an external pm-ops can mask an incomplete local install. Cleared ambient NODE_PATH in the fixture helper; the explicit looping-path fixture keeps its own path. Hostile-environment launcher suite now passes 8/8, zero skips; duplication remains zero. Corrected the linked package.json note through pm files to state fast-glob 3.3.3 remains and full audit has four high dev-only reports; current actual_result already states NOT READY. No historical tracker rows were rewritten."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:25:25.306Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Review correction validation: the full flock-serialized npm run release:check re-run passes 232/232 with zero skips, unchanged coverage and zero duplication. The linked hostile NODE_PATH launcher run passes 8/8. Corrected package file note is current, including fast-glob retained and full npm audit blocked. No threshold/ignore/skip changes. Portable junction fixtures tested on Linux; Windows runner unavailable. Core package dogfood remains unchanged and passed on npx/bunx."
  - created_at: "2026-10-04T11:51:31.782Z"
    author: codex-sol
    text: "Final health receipt correction: the complete pinned receipt has TWO advisory categories, stale_in_progress_items:2 and provenance_value_domain_invalid:claude-code:role:single_digit:43. The earlier shortened resumption summary omitted the latter. Health exits 0 with no gate-failing findings. Historical provenance reporting is tracked separately for assessment; audit markers are preserved. Package code, gates, 232/232 full test result and packed dogfood are unchanged; full npm audit still blocks certification on four high dev-only reports."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T19:28:54.926Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Tracker reconciliation correction: main 80717afb81f1 contains PR #128 (9a772c1c667f), which delivered the dated PM CLI/SDK 2026.10.4 toolchain update. The retained audit, health and review receipts do not establish completed certification. Later toolchain updates and PR #141 remediation are separate evidence. The prior completed-certification wording and closure are superseded; certification remains unestablished. Scope: tracker state only; no new runtime certification or deployment claim."
    edited_at: "2026-10-22T11:12:49.573Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T11:12:37.531Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "PR 163 review: remote head pulled; main 80717afb81f1 is already an ancestor, and the initial worktree had no unpublished commits or edits. Read all comments in four unresolved threads and latest CodeRabbit body; no outside-diff findings. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vB4sY and PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vB4sg are valid: PR #128 delivered the dated toolchain update, but retained receipts explicitly say NOT READY. Reopened this certification item rather than recording acceptance from ancestry. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vB4sk and PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vB4sm are valid: dependency-removal evidence and changelog wording need correction. Severity is minor and tracker-only. Preserve every existing history record and append all corrections with the pinned CLI; no runtime certification or gate-threshold changes."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T11:13:08.673Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "Evidence recheck and same-class self-review: all 11 reconciliation items were compared with main 80717afb81f1. Delivery commits 9a772c1c667f, afd01629ede3, a61eb3953e2c, d19cca2d2a2b, 6b0eb38f75bc and 37452470fbc4 remain ancestors. Both GitHub workflow callers retain 67a5e3e / 2026.10.16; CodeQL registration, OIDC/pre-bump release guards, deterministic changelog flags and attestation consumer remain present. PR #122 is closed and its duplicate remains canceled. Triplicate implementation delivery does not certify the separately recorded pending native Inkscape acceptance. No additional false completed-certification claim found. Both new audit scopes report zero vulnerabilities. All 11 changed history streams preserve their complete main prefix; corrections append after the original PR close event, which remains byte-identical. The reopened certification item has no closed/completed timestamps or close_reason; the false closed record is superseded, not rewritten."
  - created_at: "2026-10-22T11:16:19.487Z"
    author: codex-agent
    text: "PR 163 final tracker-only proof: main 80717afb81f1 and its retained mdm1 receipt explicitly leave dated 2026.10.4 certification NOT READY; PR #128 is recorded as toolchain delivery only. Materialized reconciliation comment corrected through a new append-only event; original close event retained verbatim. Reopened state has no close_reason/closed_at/completed_at. PR #141 remediation receipt, current lockfile and fresh full/production audit zero establish the dependency replacement; e7rd title/result/description/closure and regenerated changelog now describe delivered removal. All 11 changed history streams preserve both the complete main prefix and complete original PR-head prefix. This main-evidence recheck replaces behavioral revert tests for a tracker-only change. npm ci passed (133 packages, zero vulnerabilities); both audit scopes zero; pm test --run --progress --match=\"git show origin/main:\" --timeout 1200 passed 2/2 evidence commands. npm run changelog:full and changelog:check passed. Isolated pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passed all gate requirements with no history drift; only non-failing stale-item, historical-provenance and transient telemetry-queue advisories were reported. No runtime/source/dist/dependency/threshold change, thread reply/resolution, mention, merge or release. No new PM CLI/SDK defect encountered. Keep certification in progress and release ownership for orchestrator verification."
